{"name":"Aeronautic","hex":"#2b3448","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aeronautic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having to do with aerial navigation"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aeronautic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aeronautics","blocks":[{"text":"Aeronautics is the science or art involved with the study, design, and manufacturing of air flight-capable machines, and the techniques of operating aircraft and rockets within the atmosphere. \nWhile the term originally referred solely to operating the aircraft, it has since been expanded to include technology, business, and other aspects related to aircraft. The term \"aviation\" is sometimes used interchangeably with aeronautics, although \"aeronautics\" includes lighter-than-air craft such as airships, and includes ballistic vehicles while \"aviation\" technically does not."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/NHIndustries_NH90_at_Paris_Air_Show_2025_%283%29.jpg/330px-NHIndustries_NH90_at_Paris_Air_Show_2025_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aeronautics"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Air_France%2C_Airbus_A380-861%2C_F-HPJA.jpg/500px-Air_France%2C_Airbus_A380-861%2C_F-HPJA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Air_France%2C_Airbus_A380-861%2C_F-HPJA.jpg/1280px-Air_France%2C_Airbus_A380-861%2C_F-HPJA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Air_France%2C_Airbus_A380-861%2C_F-HPJA.jpg/500px-Air_France%2C_Airbus_A380-861%2C_F-HPJA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Air France, Airbus A380-861, F-HPJA","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAir_France%2C